cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this helped, cite it."
type: software
title: "514.48 on Jumper-v0 without jumping: a contact loophole in Evolution Gym"
abstract: "A two-cell robot scores 514.48 on Evolution Gym's Jumper-v0 by falling through the floor and being thrown out by it. An estimated 97% of the score comes from an unhandled case in the simulator's contact routine; with that case closed the best design found scores 13.83. The same robot, unchanged, also reaches the top of Climber-v0 and Climber-v1. The repository holds the designs, a step-by-step energy account, the patch, replays of the robots the benchmark's authors released, and a check that reproduces every number."
authors:
